course: dictionary
lesson: 9288
title: Words that shine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Look at this sentence: «On Romilly's court day she wears her sparkly shoes.» The word sparkly is describing shoes, so think about what shoes look like when they catch the light. Sparkly means shining with lots of tiny flashes of light, like glitter.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «On Romilly's court day she wears her shining shoes» still makes sense, so you have the right idea. Sparkly is shining with many tiny flashes, not just one plain shine.
explain: Words can also describe people and drinks. A "sparkly personality" means someone lively, bright and full of fun. Sparkly drinks are fizzy ones. Read the words around the word to decide which meaning fits: shoes and dresses mean shining, but a personality means fun.
fact: Sparkly means shining with lots of tiny flashes of light, like glitter, sequins, frost or diamonds.
fact: «Sparkly» can also mean lively, bright and full of fun, as in "a sparkly personality".
fact: Informally, «sparkly» drinks are fizzy ones.
fact: The comparative forms are sparklier (more sparkly) and sparkliest (most sparkly).
fact: Common phrases include "sparkly dress", "sparkly shoes" and "sparkly eyes".
exercise: «On Romilly's court day she wears her sparkly shoes.» What does sparkly mean here? | *Shining with tiny flashes of light | Dirty and muddy | Quiet and still | Very heavy
exercise: Ben says, "Her sparkly personality makes everyone smile." What does sparkly mean here? | *Lively, bright and full of fun | Covered in glitter | Old and worn | Fizzy
exercise: Which of these is best described as sparkly? | *A frosty field with tiny points of light on a winter morning | A quiet, empty room | A bowl of cold soup | A plain grey stone
test: Which word is the comparative of sparkly, meaning shinier with more tiny flashes? | sparkliest | *sparklier | sparklish | sparklyer
test: «The children's sparkly drinks fizzed in their glasses.» What does sparkly mean in this sentence? | Lively and full of fun | Cold and sweet | Shining with glitter | *Fizzy
exam: Which sentence uses sparkly to mean lively and full of fun? | She wore a sparkly red hat. | *Everyone loved his sparkly sense of humour at the party. | The sparkly diamonds sat in the box. | The sparkly frost covered the grass.
